{"text": "ABERNETHY-RUIZ DEFENSE, PLLC\nCASE NOTES -- PRIVILEGED / WORK PRODUCT\n\nClient:   Hunter Brannigan   DOB 09/27/1991\nCourt:    Flagstaff Justice Court, Coconino County, No. CR-2026-004417\nCitation: AZ0301-7781245\nCharges:  A.R.S. § 28-1381(A)(1) (impaired to slightest degree), A.R.S. § 28-1382 (extreme)\nAtty:     Colleen Abernethy-Ruiz (CAR), State Bar No. 031774\n\n6/8/26 -- initial consult (CAR)\nHunter was stopped Saturday May 30, 2026 around 11:40 pm on\nRoute 66 near Fanning Drive by DPS Trooper Dale Yazzie, badge #6193, for\ndrifting over the fog line. He was driving his own truck, a 2017 three-quarter-ton\npickup, AZ plate CKD7R42, VIN 1FT7W2BT4HEC30918. Passenger was his girlfriend,\nGeorgia Tsosie. Yazzie says odor of alcohol, bloodshot eyes, six of six\nclues on HGN. Hunter says he had \"three beers at Georgia's cousin's\ngraduation\" and that the field tests were done on a gravel shoulder in the wind.\n\nBreath test on the Intoxilyzer 9000 at the Coconino County jail: 0.158 and\n0.151, 12:52 and 12:59 am. That is extreme by a hair. Need the\nmaintenance and calibration logs and the 15-minute deprivation video.\n\nPriors: one prior DUI in 2019 in Mohave County (pled to regular DUI, completed\nclasses). That is within 84 months, so this is charged as a second offense.\nExposure is real jail. Also on file: a 2012 juvenile adjudication for shoplifting,\nnot usable.\n\nHealth: Hunter is a Type 1 diabetic on an insulin pump. He says his\nsugar was low that night (he read 58 on his meter at the jail) and nobody\nwould let him eat. Hypoglycemia can mimic impairment and ketones can affect some\nbreath machines; ask Dr. Quintero (Raúl Quintero, endocrinology) for\nrecords and whether he will testify. Pump serial no. NG2187443H in case we\nneed the data download.\n\nWork: he holds a CDL (AZ license D08841276) and drives belly dumps for\nPonderosa Aggregate Hauling LLC. A conviction means a one-year CDL\ndisqualification even though he was in his personal vehicle. His dispatcher,\nWendell Begaye, does not know yet. Hunter is an enrolled member of the Navajo Nation\nand asked about treatment options through tribal services; will check.\n\nTruck was towed to High Country Towing & Recovery, 4410 E. Huntington Dr., lot\nticket HC-118834. Storage is running $45 a day. 30-day impound unless\nwe get an early release hearing.\n\nMVD: admin per se suspension. He was handed the pink Form 40-5807 on 5/31/26; the 15-day\nwindow to request a hearing ends June 15. FILE THE HEARING REQUEST MONDAY.\n\n6/9/26 -- CAR\nDiscovery request under Rule 15.1 sent. Body-cam is on the state portal:\nhttps://evidence.azdps.example/share/7f3a91c2   login car_defense / pw Monsoon#2291\nWatched the first 20 min. No Miranda before the \"how much have you had\" questions\nat the tailgate, but he was not in custody yet. Yazzie tells Hunter to \"quit\nfidgeting with that thing on your belt\" -- that is the pump. Good for us.\n\nMs. Tsosie called (nine two eight, 555-0164). She will say he seemed fine but\nshaky. She does not want to testify if her ex finds out where she was.\n\nFees: flat $6,000 through trial in justice court, 2,500 paid on 6/8/26\n(Visa ending 8203), balance in three payments. Bond was $1,500 cash,\nposted by his mother.\n\nIf convicted he will need an interlock for 12 months. SafeStart Interlock of Northern Arizona\nquoted $89/mo. Client contact: hbrannigan91@postbox.example, cell 928.555.0137.\nMail to PO Box 2204, Bellemont, AZ 86015.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "555 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Hunter Brannigan", "Georgia Tsosie", "Colleen Abernethy-Ruiz", "Dale Yazzie", "Wendell Begaye", "Raúl Quintero", "Ms. Tsosie", "Hunter", "Yazzie", "Monsoon"], "companies": ["ABERNETHY-RUIZ DEFENSE", "Intoxilyzer", "Ponderosa Aggregate Hauling LLC", "Navajo Nation", "High Country Towing & Recovery", "SafeStart Interlock of Northern Arizona"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Fanning Drive", "Route 66", "Coconino County", "Jail", "High Country Towing & Recovery", "Bellemont", "Arizona", "North Arizona"], "health": ["Type 1 diabetic", "insulin pump", "sugar was low", "hypoglycemia", "ketones", "CDL", "diabetes", "suspension", "Shaky"], "sensitive": [], "names": ["Hunter", "Georgia", "Dale", "Colleen", "Raúl", "Wendell", "Yazzie", "Ms. Tsosie"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.10000000149011612, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 28, "text": "ABERNETHY-RUIZ DEFENSE, PLLC", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "ABERNETHY-RUIZ DEFENSE, PLLC"}, {"start": 80, "end": 96, "text": "Hunter Brannigan", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Hunter Brannigan"}, {"start": 103, "end": 113, "text": "09/27/1991", "kind": "dob", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "09/27/1991"}, {"start": 124, "end": 133, "text": "Flagstaff", "kind": "places", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "Flagstaff"}, {"start": 149, "end": 164, "text": "Coconino County", "kind": "places", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "Coconino County"}, {"start": 170, "end": 184, "text": "CR-2026-004417", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "CR-2026-004417"}, {"start": 195, "end": 209, "text": "AZ0301-7781245", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "AZ0301-7781245"}, {"start": 312, "end": 334, "text": "Colleen Abernethy-Ruiz", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Colleen Abernethy-Ruiz"}, {"start": 336, "end": 339, "text": "CAR", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Colleen Abernethy-Ruiz"}, {"sta